  "synthetic: no footage, a fetcher charging 2 ms a frame and nothing else. What is measured is which declaration the scheduler picks; a real decoder would lay a seek/step distribution over an effect that is about ordering.",
  "topology: one ORDERED node arming 60 rows at once at DEFERRED, against a person scrubbing without pause \u2014 a 40-row INTERACTIVE declaration re-stated every 20 ms at a new position, so it is always unserved and always outranks. 3.0 s per arm.",
  "prior art: the subsumption rule this starves under is anticipatory scheduling (Iyer & Druschel, SOSP 2001); the expiry queue that repairs it is the deadline family's anti-starvation half, drained in a batch after `fifo_batch`.",
